# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0

# Build-context filter for Dockerfile beside it (BuildKit reads the
# <Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile; paths are relative to
# the build context, which is the repository root).
#
# Everything out, then what the build reads back in: cargo resolves the whole
# workspace even for one package, so every member's manifest and sources must
# be present, but docs, assets, release archives and above all the
# multi-gigabyte target/ must not ride along as context.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!apps
!crates
!third-party
!scripts/setup/fetch-third-party.sh

# Not cargo workspace members (Gradle and Xcode build them), and the Android
# tree's build output alone runs to gigabytes.
apps/android
apps/ios
apps/macos

# Fetched inside the image from the pins, never taken from the host: a local
# copy may be stale or edited.
third-party/crates
third-party/sherpa-onnx

# Build output; never context.
**/target
